  "text_pages": [
    "New Policy of Mandatory National Health Insurance for All International Students | 중앙대학교 국제교류팀\nGlobal Gateway\nCAU\nExchange Program\nHOME\nExchange Program\n소개\n협정대학\nExchange Program\n파견 프로그램\nShort-Term Program\n단기 프로그램\nNotice\nNotice\nOverview\nAdmission Procedures\nVisa & Immigration\nHousing & Life\nNotice\n공유\n공지\nNew Policy of Mandatory National Health Insurance for All International Students\n조회수 36529\n관리자\n2021.03.02\nThe National insurance policy that applies\nto all international students (including exchange students) studying in Korea\nhas changed as of March 1st, 2021.\nBefore this change, international students\nhad to personally purchase their insurance and prepare themselves for potential\naccidents or injuries.\nHowever, from March 1st, 2021, all\ninternational students with D-2 visas who are given ARC numbers by the\nImmigration Office are automatically subject to mandatory subscription of the\nNational Health Insurance Service, provided by the Korean government.\nIf international students do not pay their\nfee for the National Health Insurance Service, they will face disadvantages,\nspecifically restrictions on immigration applications such as visa extension,\netc.\nFurthermore, international students should\nconsider that Korean nationals also purchase multiple insurances in addition to\nthe National Health Insurance Service, to ensure that they are fully covered in\ncase of national disasters or accidents.\nPlease make sure you have a comprehensive\nunderstanding of the above information, and we would appreciate your full\ncooperation and kind understanding regarding this change in the national insurance\npolicy.\nBelow are links of informative videos provided by the National Health Insurance Service.\nhttps://youtu.be/IxAT_04aieM\n(Korean)\nhttps://youtu.be/cUC3B0BnJ5U\n(Eng)\nhttps://youtu.be/cLK7_lPAUR8\n(Chinese)\nOffice\nof International Affairs\n목록\n이전글\n이전글이 없습니다.\n다음글\nAnnouncement of Punishment for Violation of Regulations during Examination\nExchange Program\nNotice\nOverview\nAdmission Procedures\nVisa & Immigration\nHousing & Life"
  ],
